  "notes": "USAGE:\nOne of several かえる verbs that learners often confuse. The key distinction:\n- {換|か}える: to exchange or convert (swap A for B of comparable value)\n- {変|か}える: to change, to alter (transform the nature of something)\n- {代|か}える: to substitute (use B in place of A)\n- {替|か}える: to replace (put a new one where the old one was)\n\n{換|か}える emphasizes the idea of exchange or conversion, especially when value is preserved. It is most natural with currency, units of measurement, and tradeable items.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {両替|りょうがえ}: currency exchange (noun form using the same kanji concept)\n- {換算|かんさん}する: to convert (units, figures)\n- {換気|かんき}する: to ventilate (exchange air)\n- ポイントを{換|か}える: to redeem points",
